25;\r\n&#2348;&#2396;&#2375;-&#2348;&#2396;&#2375;\r\n&#2337;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360; &#2324;&#2352;\r\n&#2309;&#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375;\r\n&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360;\r\n&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375;\r\n&#2332;&#2352;&#2370;&#2352;&#2340;&#2350;&#2306;&#2342;\r\n&#2350;&#2352;&#2368;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;\r\n&#2360;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;\r\n&#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366;\r\n&#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2325;&#2352;\r\n&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2332;&#2344;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2339;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;\r\n&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375;\r\n&#2354;&#2366;&#2349;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340;\r\n&#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404; &#2350;&#2361;&#2379;&#2342;&#2351;,\r\n&#2350;&#2376;&#2306; &#2342;&#2375;&#2358; &#2349;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375;\r\n&#2321;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2350;&#2368;\r\n&#2350;&#2352;&#2368;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2311;&#2360;\r\n&#2360;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;\r\n&#2342;&#2375;&#2326;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319;\r\n&#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2375;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368;\r\n&#2325;&#2366;\r\n&#2360;&#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2370;&#2340;&#2367;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325;\r\n&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375;\r\n&#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;\r\n&#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2352;&#2379;&#2343; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366;\r\n&#2361;&#2370;&#2306;&#2404; \n(&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340;)"],["Reply","No Reply"]],"links":[{"label":"Official source","url":"https://rsdoc.nic.in/memberGetdata/Get_SpecialMentionmemberwise?mpcode=2510"}]},{"title":"Demand to declare Assamese language as a classical language of India.","date":"2022-12-16","details":[["Date","16/12/2022"],["Session","258"],["Ministry","HOME AFFAIRS"],["Statement","SHRI PABITRA\r\nMARGHERITA (Assam):Thank\r\nyou, Vice-Chairman Sir. With your permission, I would like to speak in\r\nAssamese. I also thank this august House for having the facility of Assamese to\r\nEnglish interpretation. \nMy\r\nsubject pertains to an appeal to declare Assamese language as a classical\r\nlanguage of India. *\"Among the\r\nlanguages included in the larger Indo-European linguistic family, Assamese is\r\nan ancient language that is recognized by the Indian Constitution and spoken by\r\nabout 23 million people. \nMultiple States in the North-Eastern India have been\r\nusing Assamese as the lingua franca.\r\nThis language has continuous history of about 2,000 years. Along with the\r\ndevelopment of the language, examples of literary work in Assamese have been\r\nfound since the eighty-ninth century BC. The most important aspect is Ramayana\r\nwas translated into Assamese language ? the first translation of the epic in\r\nany language in the Northern part of India ? way back in 14th\r\ncentury by Madhav Kandali. Considering the glorious history of the language and\r\nits literature, Assamese is eligible for being recognized as a classical Indian\r\nlanguage alongside the six already-recognized classical languages because\r\nAssamese language fulfils all the criteria required for this recognition. Under\r\nthe leadership of hon. Assam Chief Minister Himanta Biswa Sarma, academic\r\nmeasures have already been initiated for this. Therefore, I appeal for steps\r\nfrom the Central Government to recognize Assamese as a classical\r\nlanguage.\" \n(Ends)"],["Reply","No Reply"]],"links":[{"label":"Official source","url":"https://rsdoc.nic.in/memberGetdata/Get_SpecialMentionmemberwise?mpcode=2510"}]}]}